  "prompt": "Which 2025 promotions earned less gross margin than their baseline? For each promotion that started in 2025 (start_date from 1 January to 31 December 2025), compare the units and the gross margin on promotion with the baseline's, and keep the promotions whose margin on promotion is below the baseline's margin. A line's gross margin is its net_revenue_eur minus units times unit_cost_eur. A sales line is on a promotion when it carries that promotion's ID in order_lines.promo_id, whatever its date; where two promotions overlap on a product, a line carries only the deeper one, so it counts once. The baseline ends the day before the promotion's start_date and has as many days as the promotion ran, start_date and end_date both counted; it holds every sales line of the promotion's products in those days, whatever promotion the line carries. Days are sales.order_date, the UTC day of the order. A period with no sale counts 0. Return three columns, in this order: promo_id, uplift_units (units on promotion minus baseline units) and uplift_margin (margin on promotion minus baseline margin). Return one row for each promotion kept. Any row order is fine.",
  "output_contract": {
    "columns": [
      {
        "name": "promo_id",
        "type_class": "numeric"
      },
      {
        "name": "uplift_units",
